IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `fwa-employee`
IMPORT `fwa-general-protections`

-- Fair Work Act 2009, the general protections for a dismissed employee and the one-claim-at-a-time rules -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case. Expected results were written by hand from the text.
--
-- The facts are the first matter of the route chooser (workbench consoles/route-chooser/DESIGN.md, matter
-- au/vic/route-chooser-marsh), not a cradle-to-grave life. Lena Marsh, 41, a warehouse coordinator in Dandenong,
-- Victoria, for Brightwater Logistics Pty Ltd (about 120 employees), employed since March 2022 on $78,000 a year, tells
-- her manager in August 2026 that she has multiple sclerosis and asks for changed shifts; she is dismissed with effect on
-- 2 October 2026 for "performance", and first sees a lawyer on day 25. The matter is FICTIONAL; cases marked
-- HYPOTHETICAL change her facts to reach another branch of a rule.

§ `Adverse action, workplace rights and the presumed reason`

-- s 342(1) item 1. Lena (dismissed); nothing done; a pay cut only (HYPOTHETICAL).
#ASSERT `Has my employer taken adverse action against me` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Has my employer taken adverse action against me` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Has my employer taken adverse action against me` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE

-- s 341(1). Lena is entitled to the NES under the Act, and her request for changed shifts is a process under it.
#ASSERT `Do I have a workplace right` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Do I have a workplace right` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

-- s 361. Lena alleges disability was a reason and asks for final orders: her employer must disprove it.
#ASSERT `Must my employer prove it did not act for that reason` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Must my employer prove it did not act for that reason` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Must my employer prove it did not act for that reason` FALSE FALSE

-- ss 360, 361. Not disproved: taken as a reason. Disproved: not. Interim injunction only: no presumption.
#ASSERT `Is the reason I allege taken to be one of its reasons` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Is the reason I allege taken to be one of its reasons` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Is the reason I allege taken to be one of its reasons` TRUE TRUE FALSE

§ `Sections 340, 351 and 352`

-- s 340(1). Lena: dismissed, with a workplace right (the shift request) among the reasons; then with it not a reason.
#ASSERT `Did my employer breach the workplace rights protection` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Did my employer breach the workplace rights protection` TRUE TRUE FALSE

-- s 351. Lena: dismissal, disability among the reasons, unlawful under the Equal Opportunity Act 2010 (Vic) (an input
-- here: that Act is another subject, which the stable l4 cannot IMPORT). Then the three exceptions in s 351(2), each HYPOTHETICAL.
#ASSERT `Did my employer breach the discrimination protection` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Did my employer breach the discrimination protection` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Did my employer breach the discrimination protection` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Did my employer breach the discrimination protection` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE

-- s 352 with reg 3.01 (all HYPOTHETICAL: Lena was not dismissed for an absence).
-- Five days off with a medical certificate the next morning, dismissed for it.
#ASSERT `Was I protected from dismissal for being away ill or injured` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- Four months off, sick leave ran out after six weeks: reg 3.01(5) takes the protection away.
#ASSERT NOT `Was I protected from dismissal for being away ill or injured` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- Four months off, all of it on paid personal leave: still protected.
#ASSERT `Was I protected from dismissal for being away ill or injured` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- Several absences adding up to more than 3 months in a year, not all on paid leave: not protected.
#ASSERT NOT `Was I protected from dismissal for being away ill or injured` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE
-- No certificate, declaration, instrument notice or leave evidence: not a prescribed illness.
#ASSERT NOT `Was I protected from dismissal for being away ill or injured` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- Evidence given for personal leave instead of a certificate: prescribed (reg 3.01(4)).
#ASSERT `Was I protected from dismissal for being away ill or injured` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE

§ `Time limits: Lena on day 25`

-- s 366: 21 days. Lena on day 25 is out of time unless the FWC finds exceptional circumstances.
#ASSERT NOT `Am I in time to apply to the FWC about the dismissal` 25 FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I in time to apply to the FWC about the dismissal` 25 TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I in time to apply to the FWC about the dismissal` 21 FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Am I in time to apply to the FWC about the dismissal` 22 FALSE
-- The same 21 days for unfair dismissal (s 394(2), in fwa-employee.l4): both Fair Work doors shut together on day 22.
#ASSERT NOT `Am I in time to apply for unfair dismissal` 25 FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I in time to apply for unfair dismissal` 21 FALSE

-- s 370: 14 days from the certificate, or an interim injunction (HYPOTHETICAL timings).
#ASSERT `May I take my dismissal claim to court` TRUE 10 FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `May I take my dismissal claim to court` TRUE 14 FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `May I take my dismissal claim to court` TRUE 15 FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `May I take my dismissal claim to court` TRUE 15 TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `May I take my dismissal claim to court` FALSE 0 FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `May I take my dismissal claim to court` FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE

-- s 369(1): arbitration needs the certificate, both parties, 14 days, the rules, and no other live dismissal claim.
#ASSERT `Can the FWC arbitrate my dismissal dispute` TRUE TRUE 7 FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Can the FWC arbitrate my dismissal dispute` TRUE TRUE 7 FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Can the FWC arbitrate my dismissal dispute` TRUE TRUE 20 FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Can the FWC arbitrate my dismissal dispute` TRUE FALSE 7 FALSE TRUE FALSE

§ `Costs`

-- s 611: each side bears its own costs at the FWC unless one of the two findings is made.
#ASSERT NOT `Can the FWC order me to pay costs` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the FWC order me to pay costs` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the FWC order me to pay costs` FALSE TRUE

-- s 570: in court, only for vexatious or unreasonable conduct, or an unreasonable refusal at the FWC on the same facts.
#ASSERT NOT `Can a court order me to pay costs of a Fair Work claim` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Can a court order me to pay costs of a Fair Work claim` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Can a court order me to pay costs of a Fair Work claim` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Can a court order me to pay costs of a Fair Work claim` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Can a court order me to pay costs of a Fair Work claim` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE

§ `One dismissal claim at a time`

`Lena's AHRC complaint about the dismissal` MEANS `Earlier claim` WITH
    `its kind` IS `a complaint under another law (s 732)`
    `it is about the dismissal` IS TRUE
    `it is only about benefits owed because of the dismissal` IS FALSE
    `I withdrew it` IS FALSE
    `it failed for want of jurisdiction` IS FALSE
    `the FWC issued its certificate` IS FALSE
    `the parties then agreed to FWC arbitration` IS FALSE
    `it failed because the FWC found a genuine redundancy` IS FALSE

-- s 732(3): a complaint about the shifts alone does not yet relate to the dismissal.
`Lena's AHRC complaint about the shifts only` MEANS `Earlier claim` WITH
    `its kind` IS `a complaint under another law (s 732)`
    `it is about the dismissal` IS FALSE
    `it is only about benefits owed because of the dismissal` IS FALSE
    `I withdrew it` IS FALSE
    `it failed for want of jurisdiction` IS FALSE
    `the FWC issued its certificate` IS FALSE
    `the parties then agreed to FWC arbitration` IS FALSE
    `it failed because the FWC found a genuine redundancy` IS FALSE

`Lena's general protections application, in conference` MEANS `Earlier claim` WITH
    `its kind` IS `a general protections application to the FWC (s 727)`
    `it is about the dismissal` IS TRUE
    `it is only about benefits owed because of the dismissal` IS FALSE
    `I withdrew it` IS FALSE
    `it failed for want of jurisdiction` IS FALSE
    `the FWC issued its certificate` IS FALSE
    `the parties then agreed to FWC arbitration` IS FALSE
    `it failed because the FWC found a genuine redundancy` IS FALSE

`Lena's general protections application, certificate issued` MEANS `Earlier claim` WITH
    `its kind` IS `a general protections application to the FWC (s 727)`
    `it is about the dismissal` IS TRUE
    `it is only about benefits owed because of the dismissal` IS FALSE
    `I withdrew it` IS FALSE
    `it failed for want of jurisdiction` IS FALSE
    `the FWC issued its certificate` IS TRUE
    `the parties then agreed to FWC arbitration` IS FALSE
    `it failed because the FWC found a genuine redundancy` IS FALSE

`Lena's general protections application, arbitration agreed` MEANS `Earlier claim` WITH
    `its kind` IS `a general protections application to the FWC (s 727)`
    `it is about the dismissal` IS TRUE
    `it is only about benefits owed because of the dismissal` IS FALSE
    `I withdrew it` IS FALSE
    `it failed for want of jurisdiction` IS FALSE
    `the FWC issued its certificate` IS TRUE
    `the parties then agreed to FWC arbitration` IS TRUE
    `it failed because the FWC found a genuine redundancy` IS FALSE

`an unfair dismissal application on foot` MEANS `Earlier claim` WITH
    `its kind` IS `an unfair dismissal application (s 729)`
    `it is about the dismissal` IS TRUE
    `it is only about benefits owed because of the dismissal` IS FALSE
    `I withdrew it` IS FALSE
    `it failed for want of jurisdiction` IS FALSE
    `the FWC issued its certificate` IS FALSE
    `the parties then agreed to FWC arbitration` IS FALSE
    `it failed because the FWC found a genuine redundancy` IS FALSE

`an unfair dismissal application withdrawn` MEANS `Earlier claim` WITH
    `its kind` IS `an unfair dismissal application (s 729)`
    `it is about the dismissal` IS TRUE
    `it is only about benefits owed because of the dismissal` IS FALSE
    `I withdrew it` IS TRUE
    `it failed for want of jurisdiction` IS FALSE
    `the FWC issued its certificate` IS FALSE
    `the parties then agreed to FWC arbitration` IS FALSE
    `it failed because the FWC found a genuine redundancy` IS FALSE

`an unfair dismissal application that failed on genuine redundancy` MEANS `Earlier claim` WITH
    `its kind` IS `an unfair dismissal application (s 729)`
    `it is about the dismissal` IS TRUE
    `it is only about benefits owed because of the dismissal` IS FALSE
    `I withdrew it` IS FALSE
    `it failed for want of jurisdiction` IS FALSE
    `the FWC issued its certificate` IS FALSE
    `the parties then agreed to FWC arbitration` IS FALSE
    `it failed because the FWC found a genuine redundancy` IS TRUE

`an unfair dismissal application that failed for want of jurisdiction` MEANS `Earlier claim` WITH
    `its kind` IS `an unfair dismissal application (s 729)`
    `it is about the dismissal` IS TRUE
    `it is only about benefits owed because of the dismissal` IS FALSE
    `I withdrew it` IS FALSE
    `it failed for want of jurisdiction` IS TRUE
    `the FWC issued its certificate` IS FALSE
    `the parties then agreed to FWC arbitration` IS FALSE
    `it failed because the FWC found a genuine redundancy` IS FALSE

-- s 733: a claim only for the entitlements owed on dismissal is not a claim "in relation to a dismissal".
`a complaint only about unpaid entitlements on dismissal` MEANS `Earlier claim` WITH
    `its kind` IS `a complaint under another law (s 732)`
    `it is about the dismissal` IS TRUE
    `it is only about benefits owed because of the dismissal` IS TRUE
    `I withdrew it` IS FALSE
    `it failed for want of jurisdiction` IS FALSE
    `the FWC issued its certificate` IS FALSE
    `the parties then agreed to FWC arbitration` IS FALSE
    `it failed because the FWC found a genuine redundancy` IS FALSE

-- ss 726-733: which earlier claims still count.
#ASSERT `Does this earlier claim still count` `Lena's AHRC complaint about the dismissal`
#ASSERT NOT `Does this earlier claim still count` `Lena's AHRC complaint about the shifts only`
#ASSERT `Does this earlier claim still count` `Lena's general protections application, in conference`
#ASSERT NOT `Does this earlier claim still count` `Lena's general protections application, certificate issued`
#ASSERT `Does this earlier claim still count` `Lena's general protections application, arbitration agreed`
#ASSERT `Does this earlier claim still count` `an unfair dismissal application on foot`
#ASSERT NOT `Does this earlier claim still count` `an unfair dismissal application withdrawn`
#ASSERT NOT `Does this earlier claim still count` `an unfair dismissal application that failed on genuine redundancy`
#ASSERT NOT `Does this earlier claim still count` `an unfair dismissal application that failed for want of jurisdiction`
#ASSERT NOT `Does this earlier claim still count` `a complaint only about unpaid entitlements on dismissal`

-- s 725, with s 732: an AHRC complaint about the dismissal shuts both Fair Work dismissal doors, and the reverse.
#ASSERT NOT `May I make this dismissal claim` `an unfair dismissal application (s 729)` (LIST `Lena's AHRC complaint about the dismissal`)
#ASSERT NOT `May I make this dismissal claim` `a general protections application to the FWC (s 727)` (LIST `Lena's AHRC complaint about the dismissal`)
#ASSERT NOT `May I make this dismissal claim` `a complaint under another law (s 732)` (LIST `an unfair dismissal application on foot`)
#ASSERT NOT `May I make this dismissal claim` `a complaint under another law (s 732)` (LIST `Lena's general protections application, in conference`)
-- s 732(3): a complaint about the shifts alone leaves the Fair Work doors open.
#ASSERT `May I make this dismissal claim` `an unfair dismissal application (s 729)` (LIST `Lena's AHRC complaint about the shifts only`)
-- The ordinary path: after the certificate, the court application is open (s 727(1)(b)(iii)).
#ASSERT `May I make this dismissal claim` `a general protections court application (s 728)` (LIST `Lena's general protections application, certificate issued`)
-- Agreeing to arbitration shuts the court (s 727(1A)).
#ASSERT NOT `May I make this dismissal claim` `a general protections court application (s 728)` (LIST `Lena's general protections application, arbitration agreed`)
-- Withdrawing, or losing on jurisdiction or genuine redundancy, reopens the others.
#ASSERT `May I make this dismissal claim` `a general protections application to the FWC (s 727)` (LIST `an unfair dismissal application withdrawn`)
#ASSERT `May I make this dismissal claim` `a complaint under another law (s 732)` (LIST `an unfair dismissal application that failed on genuine redundancy`)
#ASSERT `May I make this dismissal claim` `a general protections application to the FWC (s 727)` (LIST `an unfair dismissal application that failed for want of jurisdiction`)
-- s 733: an entitlements-only complaint bars nothing.
#ASSERT `May I make this dismissal claim` `an unfair dismissal application (s 729)` (LIST `a complaint only about unpaid entitlements on dismissal`)
-- No earlier claim; and a second claim of the same kind, which s 725 does not reach (a reading: see NOTES.md).
#ASSERT `May I make this dismissal claim` `an unfair dismissal application (s 729)` EMPTY
#ASSERT `May I make this dismissal claim` `an unfair dismissal application (s 729)` (LIST `an unfair dismissal application on foot`)
-- One live claim among spent ones still bars.
#ASSERT NOT `May I make this dismissal claim` `an unfair dismissal application (s 729)` (LIST `an unfair dismissal application withdrawn`, `Lena's AHRC complaint about the dismissal`)

-- What s 725 leaves open.
#ASSERT `Which dismissal claims are still open to me` EMPTY EQUALS LIST `a bargaining order application (s 726)`, `a general protections application to the FWC (s 727)`, `a general protections court application (s 728)`, `an unfair dismissal application (s 729)`, `an unlawful termination application to the FWC (s 730)`, `an unlawful termination court application (s 731)`, `a complaint under another law (s 732)`
#ASSERT `Which dismissal claims are still open to me` (LIST `Lena's AHRC complaint about the dismissal`) EQUALS LIST `a complaint under another law (s 732)`
#ASSERT `Which dismissal claims are still open to me` (LIST `Lena's general protections application, in conference`) EQUALS LIST `a general protections application to the FWC (s 727)`
#ASSERT `Which dismissal claims are still open to me` (LIST `Lena's general protections application, certificate issued`) EQUALS LIST `a bargaining order application (s 726)`, `a general protections application to the FWC (s 727)`, `a general protections court application (s 728)`, `an unfair dismissal application (s 729)`, `an unlawful termination application to the FWC (s 730)`, `an unlawful termination court application (s 731)`, `a complaint under another law (s 732)`

-- s 723: a national system employee who can go to court under the general protections cannot use unlawful termination.
#ASSERT NOT `May I make an unlawful termination application` TRUE
#ASSERT `May I make an unlawful termination application` FALSE
